WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:02.200
The Marvel rumor mill never sleeps.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.359
Anonymous sources are reporting that Marvel
Studios head honcho Kevin Feige is in talks

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.700
with a young actor who has appeared in a Christopher
Nolan film for the lead role in a ​Nova​

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.700
feature.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.680
Some observers have a few ideas as to who
that might be.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.580
The rumor was reported by YouTuber TVO during
a recent episode of his video series, Lords

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.610
of the Long Box.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.190
While he didn't offer any suggestions about
the possible identity of the actor who is

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:27.500
supposedly up for the plum role, the folks
at Cosmic Book News took the rumor and identified

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.580
a few stars who have worked with Nolan, and
who physically fit the bill for the part of

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.580
Nova.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.570
Among them: Harry Styles, Fionn Whitehead,
and Barry Keoghan, all of whom appeared in

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.250
Nolan's 2017 flick Dunkirk.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.280
Also singled out as a possibility was Timothée
Chalamet, who popped up in 2014's Interstellar.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.440
Now, this would be exciting news if it turns
out to be accurate - but frankly, we have

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.440
our doubts.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.950
It must be pointed out that no Nova feature
has even been confirmed at this time.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:57.030
Still, there are a couple of strong indications
that the character is being prepped for entry

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.830
into the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.000
In case you're not familiar, the original
Nova is the heroic identity of Richard Rider,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.631
an earthling who was imbued with the power
and knowledge of the entire Nova Corps, the

00:01:06.631 --> 00:01:10.540
armed forces of the planet Xandar, when their
home planet is destroyed.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.659
As Nova, Rider has super-strength, can fly
faster than light, can generate blasts of

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:17.930
cosmic energy, and is possessed of the "Xandarian
worldmind."

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.220
Our first clue regarding the character's impending
arrival in the MCU came during Avengers: Infinity

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.970
War, when it was revealed that Xandar had
been obliterated by Thanos.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:33.520
"Thanos already has the power stone, because
he stole it last week, when he decimated Xandar."

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.950
In the comics, Rider is gifted with the collective
power of the Nova Corps by Rhomann Dey, who

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.040
was portrayed in the first Guardian film by
John C. Reilly.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.690
That means that all of the ingredients for
the creation of Nova are already present in

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.210
the MCU, which simplifies his eventual introduction
to the franchise.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.220
"He's got a codename!"

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.280
"Come on, man, it's an outlaw name."

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.220
"Relax pal, it's cool to have a code name."

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.229
Our second hint comes from none other than
Feige himself, who has teased his interest

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:02.030
in Nova on multiple occasions.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.110
As far back as April 2018, Feige told ComicBook.com:

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:09.519
"If we have a big board with a bunch of characters
that have more immediate potential, Nova is

00:02:09.519 --> 00:02:10.629
on that board.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.560
Because of the connection to the Guardians
universe, because there are more than one

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.279
examples to pull from in the comics that are
interesting."

00:02:16.279 --> 00:02:20.099
Feige also noted that the character was present
in the earliest drafts of Guardians of the

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:21.099
Galaxy.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:25.540
All of these things considered, it sure seems
like Nova's entry into the MCU is inevitable.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.569
However, there's ample reason to view this
rumor with a healthy amount of skepticism.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:33.069
The biggest problem to Nova's introduction
is that we already know every film and TV

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:37.859
series Marvel will be producing through 2021,
and Nova is not among them.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:41.819
For that matter, neither is Guardians of the
Galaxy Vol. 3, which is thought to be coming

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:46.069
in Phase 5 and which should drop sometime
in 2022 or 2023.

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:50.309
If Nova doesn't get his own solo feature right
off the bat, it's reasonable to think that

00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:51.599
he may pop up in that film.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.400
Phase 5, however, is still pretty far down
the road - and it's not likely that Feige

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.010
and Marvel would be seeking to cast the part
of Nova at this early date.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:03.409
A potential Nova solo film wouldn't even begin
production for at least a couple years, and

00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:07.900
Guardians 3 writer/director James Gunn will
be finishing up his work on The Suicide Squad

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.469
before returning to Marvel.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:13.299
With any good fortune, we'll get some hard
news regarding Nova's future involvement in

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:15.639
the MCU sooner rather than later.

00:03:15.639 --> 00:03:19.489
We'll keep our eye out for any developments,
and keep you informed.

